//@version=5
// STAR — GEX desk MECHANICS backtest (EMA stack + volume, NO gamma).
// Isolates the strippable, historically-testable part of Nick Ireland's GEX system:
//   step 5 (EMA stack = direction) + step 6 volume confirmation.
// Gamma (steps 3-4) needs live options open-interest and has NO free history, so it
// cannot be here. This only asks: does the EMA-stack + volume TRIGGER have a directional
// edge on SPY? Entry in stack direction on volume confirm; ATR stop + R-multiple target.
//
// RESULT 2026-07-03 (SPY 1h, 2015-2026, $1000-cash):
//   long+short : PF 1.005 (breakeven, 1227 trades, 35.8% win)
//   longs-only : PF 1.197 (713 trades, 38.7% win)   <- shorts are the bleeder (SPY drift)
// VERDICT: mechanics alone ~breakeven; the GAMMA overlay is the alpha (forward-tested in
// the live gex_desk scorecard, since gamma has no backtestable history). The neg-gamma
// SHORT leg is the riskiest and must be genuinely regime-gated or it bleeds.
strategy("STAR GEX mechanics: EMA stack + volume", overlay=true, initial_capital=100000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.cash, default_qty_value=1000,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.0,
     slippage=2, pyramiding=0, process_orders_on_close=true)

e8len   = input.int(8,   "EMA fast")
e21len  = input.int(21,  "EMA mid")
e50len  = input.int(50,  "EMA slow")
volMult = input.float(1.2, "Volume mult of SMA", step=0.1)
volLen  = input.int(20,  "Volume SMA len")
atrLen  = input.int(14,  "ATR len")
atrStop = input.float(1.5,"ATR stop mult", step=0.25)
targetR = input.float(2.0,"Target R", step=0.5)
allowLong  = input.bool(true,  "Longs")
allowShort = input.bool(true,  "Shorts")   // set false for the longs-only variant (PF 1.197)

e8  = ta.ema(close, e8len)
e21 = ta.ema(close, e21len)
e50 = ta.ema(close, e50len)
atr = ta.atr(atrLen)
volOk = volume >= volMult * ta.sma(volume, volLen)

stackUp   = e8 > e21 and e21 > e50 and close >= e8
stackDown = e8 < e21 and e21 < e50 and close <= e8

longSig  = allowLong  and stackUp   and volOk
shortSig = allowShort and stackDown and volOk

if strategy.position_size == 0
    if longSig
        st = close - atrStop * atr
        if st < close
            strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
            strategy.exit("Lx", from_entry="L", stop=st, limit=close + targetR * (close - st))
    else if shortSig
        st = close + atrStop * atr
        if st > close
            strategy.entry("S", strategy.short)
            strategy.exit("Sx", from_entry="S", stop=st, limit=close - targetR * (st - close))

plot(e8,  "EMA8",  color=color.aqua)
plot(e21, "EMA21", color=color.orange)
plot(e50, "EMA50", color=color.red)
